FlyWeb/docs/sync-cuenta.md §9 and §11.

- BraveSyncHandler: FlyWebAccount* messages over flyweb_sync::
  AccountService, always resolved with {ok, error, until, data}, the
  status pushed as "flyweb-account-status-changed", and the password
  strength from zxcvbn (as the password manager's weak check; only the
  minimum length is enforced).
- settings-flyweb-sync-account: the nine states of §9, none without a way
  out; create, log in, recovery key, the email-code step with resend and
  cancel, devices, password/email/key changes, leave, delete everywhere,
  scheduled deletion, the mailbox-only flows, «¿Has sido tú?» and the
  offline state. Passwords in plain inputs outside any <form>, cleared as
  soon as they are sent. Only «Combinar» on joining (C1, pending).
- Strings: English source, es and es-419 translations with the grit
  fingerprint ids; the section title becomes «Account and sync».

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
